# NOTICE — Tessera provenance

Tessera is a **fork of [Maggy](https://github.com/alinaqi/maggy)** (MIT,
Copyright (c) 2025 Ali Naqi), not an independent reimplementation. This file
records the split honestly so that anyone reading the code knows which half
they are looking at.

## What came from Maggy

The repository was seeded by importing Maggy wholesale (commit `ad19913`,
"Import Maggy baseline (pre-prune)" — 345 files). A large majority of those files
are still byte-identical to that import, though the split is much closer to even
when weighed by line count rather than by file:

- `skills/` — the skill library, and the single largest inherited component by
  any measure
- `commands/`, `rules/`, `agents/`, and roughly half of `hooks/`. Note that the
  hooks which actually **fire** live in `.claude/scripts/` and are Tessera's; the
  inherited `hooks/` tree is a separate surface
- `cortex-mcp/`, `evals/`, and `scripts/polyphony/` — inherited essentially
  untouched, and not exercised by `tessera-test`
- Part of `scripts/` — the minority by line count. In `bin/`, only the vendored
  `gemini-cli` and `qwen3` wrappers; every `tessera-*` command is Tessera's
- Several documents under `_project_specs/` that describe **Maggy's** architecture
  and roadmap, not Tessera's (`docs/` no longer carries any)

## What is original to Tessera

The governing layer — the parts that make Tessera a framework rather than a
copy — was written from scratch:

- `docs/design-principles.md` — the compounding-principles design doc
- `docs/adr/` — the Architecture Decision Records
- `docs/observatory.md`, `docs/contracts/` — the watch list and the contracts
- `scripts/gate/`, `scripts/doccheck.py`, `scripts/override/`,
  `scripts/restore/` and `bin/tessera-escalate` — the gate, doc-honesty,
  escalation, and restore-receipt machinery
- `.claude/scripts/` — every hook wired into a Tessera session
- `bin/tessera-*` — the command line, including `tessera-verify` (the adversarial
  falsifier) and `tessera-watch` (the observatory's machine-checkable triggers)
- `chaos/` — the fail-open probes, which break a component on purpose and assert
  that Tessera reports it
- `.tessera/` — the project-profile model
- `install.sh` — Tessera's self-hosting installer (see ADR-0003)

Two subsystems sit between the categories: **Mnemos** (`scripts/mnemos/`, the
memory layer) and **iCPG** (`scripts/icpg/`, the intent graph) were inherited from
Maggy and then rewritten to roughly three-quarters, so neither list above owns them
cleanly.

## Direction of dependency

Per **ADR-0003**, the dependency is inverted: **Tessera stands alone, and Maggy
(as the superset product) may embed Tessera — never the reverse.** Installing
or using Tessera does not require cloning Maggy.

## Thanks

Maggy's skills/rules/hooks architecture, its TDD-via-Stop-hook loop, and its
PreCompact recovery pattern are the foundation Tessera is built on. Credit for
those ideas belongs to Ali Naqi and Maggy's contributors.
